---
// Self-contained path diagram — no props needed
---

<div class="path-diagram">
  <h3>Three Workflow Paths</h3>

  <div class="path-row">
    <div class="path-name">Conversation path</div>
    <div class="path-steps">
      <span class="step conv">draft-user</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step conv">draft-pdr</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step conv">draft-plan</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">finalize</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">expand</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">implement</span>
    </div>
    <p class="path-desc">Have a conversation about each stage, then format it into a document. The most thorough path — every decision is discussed before being captured.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="path-row">
    <div class="path-name">Fast path</div>
    <div class="path-steps">
      <span class="step conv">draft-user</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step doc">gen-pdr</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step doc">gen-plan</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">finalize</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">expand</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">implement</span>
    </div>
    <p class="path-desc">Conversation for user requirements only. The PDR and plan are generated directly from documents — faster, but the AI makes more design decisions autonomously.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="path-row">
    <div class="path-name">Mixed path</div>
    <div class="path-steps">
      <span class="step conv">draft-user</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step mixed">draft or gen</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step mixed">draft or gen</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">finalize</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">expand</span>
      <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="step shared">implement</span>
    </div>
    <p class="path-desc">Any combination — conversation for requirements, generated PDR, conversation for plan, or vice versa. Use conversation for decisions you want to control and generation for the rest.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .path-diagram {
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .path-diagram h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .path-row {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .path-row:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .path-name {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-heading);
  }

  .path-steps {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .step {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    border: 1px solid;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .step.conv {
    color: #1a56db;
    border-color: #1a56db;
    background: #eff6ff;
  }

  .step.doc {
    color: #166534;
    border-color: #166534;
    background: #f0fdf4;
  }

  .step.shared {
    color: var(--color-heading);
    border-color: var(--color-heading);
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .step.mixed {
    color: #6d28d9;
    border-color: #6d28d9;
    background: #f5f3ff;
  }

  .arrow {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .path-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .path-diagram {
      padding: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
